# Pipeline homologation (GitHub MCP)

Repo: `wbrunoFC/carrefour`. Workflow: `e2e-android` (`.github/workflows/e2e-android.yml`).

When CI fails, user asks pipeline status, or homologation needs evidence: **do not wait for pasted logs**. Use GitHub MCP (`user-github` or project `github`) with toolset `actions`.

1. `GetMcpTools` on the GitHub server; prefer `actions_list` / `actions_get` (or `list_workflow_runs` / `get_job_logs` if those names appear).
2. List runs for `e2e-android.yml` on `main` (and open PRs). Filter failed.
3. List jobs of the failed run, then fetch job logs.
4. Quote the shortest failing line. Fix root cause. Re-check the next run.

Auth: PAT in Cursor MCP (`GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` in env for project `.cursor/mcp.json`; global `~/.cursor/mcp.json` already has GitHub). PAT needs `repo` + `workflow` (classic) or Actions read.

Never commit PATs. Never dump full logs unless asked.
